* text=auto

*.cs      text diff=csharp
*.json    text
*.md      text

# Unity text assets -- LF, and Unity's own merge tool.
# `merge=unityyamlmerge` needs a per-machine .gitconfig entry naming
# UnityYAMLMerge.exe inside the Editor install -- see issue #10.
*.unity   text eol=lf merge=unityyamlmerge
*.prefab  text eol=lf merge=unityyamlmerge
*.asset   text eol=lf merge=unityyamlmerge
*.meta    text eol=lf

# Sim content: byte-stable on every machine
content/**  text eol=lf

# The generated copy of that content inside the player. It has to be
# BYTE-IDENTICAL to the authored original -- an edit-mode test compares the two
# and the map hash is over what the parser read -- so it needs the same line
# endings, and `content/**` above does not reach it. Without this line the
# default `text=auto` would give the copy CRLF in a Windows working tree while
# the original kept LF, and a fresh clone would go red on two files nobody had
# touched. Same class of trap as the *.replay rule below: a generated file
# whose bytes a checkout may rewrite is a generated file that does not match
# what generated it.
client/Assets/StreamingAssets/**  text eol=lf

# ...except the replay bundles, which are records and not lines of text. The
# rule above would have git normalise line endings inside a run of bytes whose
# id is the hash of those bytes, so a checkout on the wrong platform would
# produce a record that no longer is the record it says it is. This line comes
# after that one on purpose: the last matching pattern wins.
#
# UNANCHORED, AND THAT IS THE FIX RATHER THAN THE SHORTHAND. It used to read
# `content/*.replay`, which contains a slash and is therefore anchored at the
# content directory -- so the golden bundles in content/golden/ matched the
# `content/**` line above instead and would have been line-ending normalised on
# checkout. A record whose bytes a checkout may rewrite is not a record.
*.replay  binary

# Binaries -- never diff, never merge
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.fbx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.wav binary
